 \\\"Treasury Bulletin\\\" for October 1948, page A-1. Similar information concerning Series C notes will be found in the \\\"Treasury Bulletin\\\" for October 1945, pages A-4 and A-5. For details concerning terms and conditions, investment yields, and tax payment or redemption values\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [828, 161, 1488, 277], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"of Series A and B, see \\\"Annual Report of the Secretary of the Treasury\\\" for 1942, pages 207 and 220, and for sales and redemptions by fiscal years and months, see \\\"Treasury Bulletin\\\" for February 1946, pages 42 and 43.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [826, 306, 1488, 538], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"In the following tables sales and redemptions of Treasury savings notes are shown at par value. Matured notes redeemed (either for cash or for tax payment) are included in the figures on redemptions. Matured notes outstanding are reflected in the interest-bearing debt until all notes of the series have matured, when they are transferred to matured debt upon which interest has ceased, in accordance with the practice of the Daily Treasury Statement.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [173, 562, 1384, 600], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"Table 1.- Summary of Sales and Redemptions by Series, Cumulative through February 28, 1950\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [665, 605, 879, 627], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"(In millions of dollars)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [76, 627, 1476, 879], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th rowspan=\\\"2\\\">Series</th><th rowspan=\\\"2\\\">Sales</th><th colspan=\\\"3\\\">Redemptions</th><th colspan=\\\"2\\\">Amount outstanding</th></tr><tr><th>Total</th><th>For cash</th><th>For taxes