-term investing. Traders use technical analysis, buy and sell on margin, and look to capture price inefficiencies.\\\",\\\"categoryIcon\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"MdOutlineToll\\\",\\\"color\\\":\\\"violet-strong\\\"},\\\"slug\\\":\\\"Trading\\\",\\\"image\\\":{\\\"altText\\\":\\\"Trading\\\",\\\"caption\\\":null,\\\"credit\\\":null,\\\"description\\\":\\\"PHOTO\\\",\\\"height\\\":null,\\\"id\\\":null,\\\"title\\\":\\\"Trading\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"IMAGE\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://cdn.britannica.com/21/235621-159-24129B3B/britannica-money-default-subject-logo-retirement.jpg\\\",\\\"width\\\":null},\\\"newTab\\\":false,\\\"noFollow\\\":false,\\\"url\\\":\\\"/money/browse/Trading\\\"},\\\"subcategories\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":13401,\\\"topCategoryId\\\":13400,\\\"title\\\":\\\"Crypto \\u0026 Foreign Exchange\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Active trading in foreign exchange (“forex”) has been around for decades, while cryptocurrencies are relative newcomers. Both track the relative value of currencies or cryptocurrencies: dollars, euro, yen, and pounds as well as Bitcoin, Ethereum, Solana, and Dogecoin.\\\",\\\"categoryIcon\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"MdOutlineToll\\\",\\\"color\\\":\\\"violet-strong\\\"},\\\"slug\\\":\\\"Crypto-Foreign-Exchange\\\",\\\"image\\\":{\\\"altText\\\":\\\"Crypto \\u0026 Foreign Exchange\\\",\\\"caption\\\":null,\\\"credit\\\":null,\\\"description\\\":\\\"PHOTO\\\",\\\"height\\\":null,\\\"id\\\":null,\\\"title\\\":\\\"Crypto \\u0026 Foreign Exchange\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"IMAGE\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://cdn.britannica.com/21/235621-159-24129B3B/britannica-money-default-subject-logo-retirement.jpg\\\",\\\"width\\\":null},\\\"newTab\\\":false,\\\"noFollow\\\":false,\\\"url\\\":\\\"/money/browse/Crypto-Foreign-Exchange\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":13402,\\\"topCategoryId\\\":13400,\\\"title\\\":\\\"Futures \\u0026 Margin Trading\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Futures contracts allow traders and investors to speculate on the direction of—and hedge underlying positions in—stock indexes, interest rates, commodities, precious metals, and more.\\\",\\\"categoryIcon\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"MdOutlineToll\\\",\\\"color\\\":\\\"violet-strong\\\"},\\\"slug\\\":\\\"Futures-Margin-Trading\\\",\\\"image\\\":{\\\"altText\\\":\\\"Futures \\u0026 Margin Trading\\\",\\\"caption\\\":null,\\\"credit\\\":null,\\\"description\\\":\\\"PHOTO\\\",\\\"height\\\":null,\\\"id\\\":null,\\\"title\\\":\\\"Futures \\u0026 Margin Trading\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"IMAGE\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://cdn.britannica.com/21/235621-159-24129B3B/britannica-money-default-subject-logo-retirement.jpg\\\",\\\"width\\\":null},\\\"newTab\\\":false,\\\"noFollow\\\":false,\\\"url\\\":\\\"/money/browse/Futures-Margin-Trading\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":13403,\\\"topCategoryId\\\":13400,\\\"title\\\":\\\"Options Trading\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Options are derivative contracts that give the buyer the right to buy or sell a security at a specific price. Options can be flexible and capital efficient. But understanding the math behind them, plus the lingo, strategies, and risk parameters, requires some training.\\\",\\\"categoryIcon\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"MdOutlineToll\\\",\\\"color\\\":\\\"violet-strong\\\"},\\\"slug\\\":\\\"Options-Trading\\\",\\\"image\\\":{\\\"altText\\\":\\\"Options Trading\\\",\\\"caption\\\":null,\\\"credit\\\":null,\\\"description\\\":\\\"PHOTO\\\",\\\"height\\\":null,\\\"id\\\":null,\\\"title\\\":\\\"Options Trading\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"IMAGE\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://cdn.britannica.com/21/235621-159-24129B3B/britannica-money-default-subject-logo-retirement.jpg\\\",\\\"width\\\":null},\\\"newTab\\\":false,\\\"noFollow\\\":false,\\\"url\\\":\\\"/money/browse/Options-Trading\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":13404,\\\"topCategoryId\\\":13400,\\\"title\\\":\\\"Technical Analysis\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Is there predictive power in price and volume data? Technical analysts watch the charts, look for patterns, and use a blend of art and science to try to optimize the timing and price levels for buy